claude-session-index provided, and this project keeps:

  - the SQLite + FTS5 session index and its schema
  - indexing of Claude Code transcripts (titles, tools, agents, topics, compaction)
  - full-text search, conversation context retrieval, analytics and synthesis
  - the "sessions" CLI shape that this project renamed to "archiver"
  - live topic capture through Claude Code hooks
  - the Claude Code skill, the LaunchAgent and the configuration layering

This project adds:

  - plan indexing: every version of every plan in ~/.claude/plans, rebuilt from
    transcripts (Write, Edit/MultiEdit, ExitPlanMode) and from the plans folder,
    with approval status and a transcript:line citation per version, linked to the
    sessions that wrote or touched them
  - folder awareness: each session's working directory, repository root, git common
    directory and branch, plus every directory a session worked in
  - project groups: one product spanning several folders, filtered with --group
  - date ranges: --from / --to on every listing and searching command, matched by
    overlap rather than start time
  - one search across sessions and plans (--in sessions | plans | all)
  - commands: groups, list --json, plans, plan, plans-for, plans export,
    hooks install | uninstall | status
  - running side by side with claude-session-index: its own command names, data home
    and hook entries, a one-time database copy (init --from-upstream) and a read-only
    topic import
  - a test suite (none existed upstream)

